        "# 5. The Machine Learning Process\n",
        "\n",
        "## Study Sheet\n",
        "\n",
        "Machine learning usually follows a process:\n",
        "\n",
        "1. **Define the problem**  \n",
        "   What are we trying to predict, classify or understand?\n",
        "\n",
        "2. **Collect data**  \n",
        "   Where does the data come from?\n",
        "\n",
        "3. **Inspect data**  \n",
        "   What columns exist? Are there missing values?\n",
        "\n",
        "4. **Clean data**  \n",
        "   Fix missing values, wrong data types and messy column names.\n",
        "\n",
        "5. **Choose features and label**  \n",
        "   Decide the inputs and the target.\n",
        "\n",
        "6. **Train the model**  \n",
        "   Let the model learn from the training data.\n",
        "\n",
        "7. **Test the model**  \n",
        "   Check how well it works on unseen data.\n",
        "\n",
        "8. **Evaluate and improve**  \n",
        "   Look at errors and limitations.\n",
        "\n",
        "9. **Explain the result**  \n",
        "   Communicate what the model can and cannot do.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Important idea\n",
        "\n",
        "A lot of machine learning work is not the model itself.  \n",
        "A lot of the work is understanding and cleaning the data."
      ],
