        "### Answers\n",
        "\n",
        "1. Explain the difference between AI and machine learning.\n",
        "Artificial Intelligence (AI) is the ability of computers or machines to perform tasks that normally require human intelligence, such as learning, problem-solving and decision-making.\n",
        "Machine Learning (ML) is a branch of AI that allows computers to learn from data and improve their performance without being explicitly programmed for every task.\n",
        "Example: AI is used in virtual assistants like Siri, while machine learning helps them recognise speech and understand commands.\n",
        "\n",
        "2. Explain the difference between supervised and unsupervised learning.\n",
        "- Supervised learning: The computer learns from labelled data, where the correct answers are already provided.\n",
        "Example: Training a model using pictures labelled as cats or dogs so it can identify them correctly.\n",
        "\n",
        "- Unsupervised learning: The computer learns from unlabelled data and identifies patterns or groups on its own.\n",
        "Example: Grouping customers according to their shopping habits without being given predefined categories.\n",
        "\n",
        "3. Why might a model trained on poor data produce poor results?\n",
        "A model trained on poor-quality data may produce inaccurate or unreliable results because the data could contain missing information, errors, duplicates or bias. The model may learn incorrect patterns and make poor predictions.\n",
